count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2456985645","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98609#issuecomment-2456985645","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98609","id":2456985645,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ScqAt","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-05T12:00:50Z","updated_at":"2024-11-05T16:25:39Z","body":"I assume half of this problem is a specification rather than a bug.\r\n\r\nWhen importing an external 3D animation, the default snap value is `1/30`, which is an unreasonable number, `0.0333`.\r\n\r\nThe problem here is that simple truncation and snapping will not allow snapping to 1.0s, so we use `modf()` snapping with https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/92670 and https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/96328 to snap every 1.0 interval.\r\n\r\nSo I think there are some possible approaches:\r\n\r\n1. Set the default for all animation modes to FPS Mode and prevent snapping to 1.0 when 0.333 is accumulated (allow accumulated error in Second mode)\r\n    - In other words, needs to add a change to #98826 to all animation default to FPS Mode\r\n2. Ignore the accumulation error issue when snapping value greater than 1.0 and document that\r\n    - In other words, #98826 only applies when step is 1.0 or higher and needs to add documentation\r\n3. Implement the \"fps compatibility mode toggle\" in Second mode in addition to approach 2\r\n    - Disable this mode allows accumulated errors in Second mode when stepping value is less than 1.0\r\n\r\nI believe that the default change by approach 1 should not be done, at least not during Godot4 (if we done it, it should do in Godot5 milestone), since it could break projects workflow that use the existing 0.0333 snap. So IMO, we should probably choose approach 2 or 3.\r\n\r\nHowever, since https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/92670 is a change made in 4.3 and not 4.2, it may still be possible to fix with approach 1 it at this time, we will discuss this later in the animation meeting @lyuma @fire.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2456985645/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]